<BaseLayout title="About — Harshaa's Originals">
  <main class="wrap page-main"><div class="page-heading enter"><span class="eyebrow">PERSONNEL FILE / 001</span><h1>The person behind<br/><em>the projects.</em></h1><p>I'm Harshaa Rajarajan. I study electrical and electronics engineering at the University of Georgia, where much of my time goes into making things and figuring out why they don't work the first time.</p></div>
    <div class="about-page-grid"><div class="portrait-placeholder"><div class="portrait-monogram">H/R</div><span>PORTRAIT / ADD YOUR PHOTO</span></div><div class="about-copy"><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT ME</span><h2>Curiosity first.</h2><p>I'm interested in work that connects hardware, software, and people. Satellites and electric vehicles are natural places for those interests to meet, but I also enjoy building smaller personal experiments.</p><p>Outside of engineering, public speaking, Model UN, and teaching have shaped the way I communicate and work with a team. I want this website to document both sides of that story.</p><p>The goal isn't to create a perfect highlight reel. It's to show the questions, design decisions, prototypes, and learning behind the things I build.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="/connect">Say hello <span>↗</span></a></div></div>
    <section class="about-values section-pad"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">HOW I THINK</span><h2>A few recurring themes.</h2></div></div><div class="value-grid"><div><span>01 / BUILD</span><h3>Make it real.</h3><p>Ideas get better when they're tested against the physical world.</p></div><div><span>02 / UNDERSTAND</span><h3>Ask why.</h3><p>A good explanation matters as much as a clever solution.</p></div><div><span>03 / COMMUNICATE</span><h3>Bring people in.</h3><p>Engineering is collaborative; clarity helps the whole team move forward.</p></div></div></section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
